course: dictionary
lesson: 7067
title: Words that tell how
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Patiently is an adverb. An adverb tells you how someone does something, and many adverbs end in -ly. Patiently tells you the way a person waits, listens or works. «His classmates listen patiently» tells you how they listen: calmly, without rushing him.
explain: Patiently means in a calm way, waiting or working without getting cross, bored or upset. Try it in a sentence: «When a classmate stammers, wait patiently and do not finish their words.» The sentence asks you to stay calm and let the other person finish, even when it takes a long time.
explain: Look for clues around the word. Words like wait, listen, explain and work often sit next to patiently. Ask yourself: is the person calm, or are they cross and rushing? If they are calm and steady, patiently fits.
fact: Patiently is an adverb, so it describes how an action is done.
fact: Patiently means calmly, without getting cross, bored or upset.
fact: Common phrases are «wait patiently», «listen patiently» and «explain patiently».
fact: Patiently comes from the word patient, which describes a calm person.
fact: A good check is to swap in a word like calmly and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «Her grandad waited patiently while she tied her shoelaces.» What does patiently mean here? | Loudly, so everyone could hear | Sadly, with his head down | Quickly, because he was in a rush | *Calmly, without getting cross
exercise: «Please explain the sum patiently to Ravi.» Which word tells you how the explaining is done? | Ravi | sum | explain | *patiently
exercise: Mia says patiently means very fast. Why is she wrong? | *Patiently means calm and not rushed | Patiently means noisy and loud | Patiently means angry and upset | Patiently means fast and busy
test: «The fisherman sat patiently by the river all afternoon.» What does patiently tell you about the fisherman? | He was fast asleep | He was shouting at the fish | *He waited calmly, without getting cross | He was in a hurry to leave
test: «When a classmate stammers, wait patiently and do not finish their words.» What should you do? | *Wait calmly and let them finish | Finish their words for them quickly | Laugh so they feel better | Walk away because they are slow
exam: Which word means nearly the same as patiently? | Loudly | Quickly | Angrily | *Calmly
